# Build artifacts
*.tsbuildinfo

# SQLite database files — local-tier substrate (Rev3-A). The DB lives
# co-located with chat-arch-data/ which is already ignored via the
# wildcard below, but the global patterns are listed explicitly so
# accidental DB files elsewhere in the tree (test scratch, dev tools)
# stay out of git. PII risk identical to the existing populated
# manifest.json — never commit a populated DB.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Claude Code per-developer state under .claude/.
#
# Use `/*` (not `/`) so git descends into the directory and honors
# the explicit negation of `.claude/settings.json` below — once the
# parent directory itself is ignored, file-level negations are
# silently dropped by git.
.claude/*
# Keep these explicitly ignored (per-developer state):
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/launch.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/projects/
# Skills folder: un-ignore the directory itself so git descends, then
# re-ignore everything inside it via `/*` so file-level negations
# below can take effect. Same trick as `.claude/*` above. Ships the
# project's own mining-pipeline skill (README references it as "the
# project's .claude/skills/mine-corrections/" and the viewer's
# dynamic topic buckets only work when the skill runs the tag-topics
# stage on every mining pass) while leaving other per-developer
# skills inside the folder ignored.
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/mine-corrections/
!.claude/skills/mine-corrections/SKILL.md
# Chat-page skill — same shape as mine-corrections. Drives the
# `/api/chat-answer` endpoint (the chat page's agent specialization),
# so it ships with the repo and not as per-developer state.
!.claude/skills/chat-answer/
!.claude/skills/chat-answer/SKILL.md
# Mine-decisions skill — Phase 2 #1 follow-up stub. The endpoint and
# UI affordance are live so it must ship with the repo even while the
# pipeline itself is unimplemented. See plan §Phase 2 #1.
!.claude/skills/mine-decisions/
!.claude/skills/mine-decisions/SKILL.md
# Curator + falsifier skills — Phase Rev3-F F1 + F2 scaffolds. Ship
# with the repo because F3+F4 kernels (and the F9 viewer-side
# PRACTICE feed) read these via `claude -p` against the contract the
# SKILL.md frontmatter pins.
!.claude/skills/curate/
!.claude/skills/curate/SKILL.md
!.claude/skills/falsify/
!.claude/skills/falsify/SKILL.md
# Narrative-mining V1 skill (drives /api/mine-narratives — the SCAN
# chain's 6th step). Per-project LLM-driven narrative synthesis.
!.claude/skills/mine-narratives/
!.claude/skills/mine-narratives/SKILL.md
# Persona-mining V1 skill (drives /api/mine-persona — the SCAN
# chain's 5th step). Ships with the repo because the endpoint +
# UI affordance depend on the contract this SKILL.md pins.
!.claude/skills/mine-persona/
!.claude/skills/mine-persona/SKILL.md
# …except (1) test fixtures, which legitimately contain a `.claude/`
# subtree that mimics what a real Cowork session directory looks
# like on disk. These are synthetic (redacted), vital for the
# exporter's cowork-source unit + integration tests, and must be
# committed so CI can see them. Both the directories AND their
# contents need the negation — a gitignored parent would otherwise
# swallow the children regardless of a `!pattern/**` rule.
!packages/exporter/test/fixtures/**/.claude/
!packages/exporter/test/fixtures/**/.claude/**
# …and (2) the project-shared Claude Code settings, which encode
# repo-wide harness rules (deny-list for `git add -A` etc.) that must
# apply to every agent / contributor cloning the repo.
!.claude/settings.json

# Design-system mirrors. The canonical files live in design-system/
# at the repo root; the standalone app's build step copies them into
# public/ for edge serving. Ignoring the mirrored copies keeps a
# single source of truth in git.
apps/standalone/public/design-system/

# Local SQLite substrate (Rev3-C). SIBLING of `public/` so the binary
# DB doesn't get served as an Astro static asset (which would expose
# the ledger and any future PII tables over HTTP). The `*.db*` globs
# above already cover the file itself; this line keeps the directory
# unstaged on a fresh clone so a `git add -A` accident can't trap it.
apps/standalone/chat-arch-data/

# Exporter output for local dev — data is on user's machine, not in repo
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/*
# Outcome-substrate sidecars (Phase 1-4) are explicitly enumerated for
# documentation — they're already covered by the wildcard above, but
# listing them keeps the PII surface auditable from .gitignore alone.
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/composite-outcomes.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/pr-land-cache.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/config-history.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/knowledge-debt.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/reflexive.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/its-analysis.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/decisions.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/archetypes.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/project-trajectories.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/surface-comparison.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/skill-curves.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/thrash-fires.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/entity-states.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/knowledge-debt-states.json
# Rev3-F curator + falsifier output. PII: narrative titles / previews
# / claim text / cited turn excerpts. Already covered by the wildcard
# above; listed for the same auditability reason as the others.
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/curator-feed.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/falsifier-verdicts.json
# Per-project persona-mining V1 output. PII: verbatim user-prompt
# excerpts cited as [SID:...] inside each per-project markdown file.
# Stage-1 candidates + Stage-2 index + per-project markdown all covered
# by the wildcard above; listed explicitly for the same auditability
# reason as the others.
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/persona-candidates.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/personas.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/personas/
# Per-project narrative-mining V1 Stage-1 sidecar. PII: verbatim
# session title + preview + summary excerpts. Stage-2 LLM rows are
# merged INTO narratives.json (the existing file gains `attributedTo:
# 'llm-derived'` rows + optional `skipped[]` / `thresholds` top-level
# fields — already covered by the wildcard above, no separate
# `narratives.json` line needed because it predates V1).
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/narrative-candidates.json
# Project Identity v2 (plan §10). Both are locally generated and PII-bearing
# (preview carries session ids + moved-session lists; overrides carry cwd
# globs / session ids). Covered by the chat-arch-data/* wildcard above; these
# explicit lines are auditable documentation per the repo convention.
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/analysis/project-identity-preview.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/projectOverrides.json
apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/exports/
.claude/review-loop.disabled
.claude/review-loop.disabled-roles
# Keep empty chat-arch-data dir on fresh clones.
!apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/.gitkeep
# Track the empty default manifest. Shipping it (instead of relying on a
# 404 for the initial empty state) forces CF Pages' edge cache to
# overwrite any previously-cached populated manifest on every deploy —
# CF auto-invalidates files it serves in the new build, but files that
# were *removed* from a build get orphaned at the edge indefinitely.
# The viewer's EmptyState path handles `sessions.length === 0` cleanly,
# so an empty manifest and a missing manifest produce the same UX
# modulo the edge-cache behavior.
!apps/standalone/public/chat-arch-data/manifest.json

# Internal scratch spaces — never ship. The three load-bearing
# planning artifacts (locked v2 spec, Rev3 plan, Rev3 progress
# tracker) are carved out so the Phase Rev3-A spec amendment can
# land as a real commit and the tracker is visible across machines /
# fresh contributors. Other planning markdown + ad-hoc scripts under
# _planning/ stay ignored.
_audit/
# Use `/*` (not `/`) so git descends into the directory and honors
# the explicit negations below — once the parent itself is ignored,
# file-level negations are silently dropped by git (same trick as
# `.claude/*` above).
_planning/*
!_planning/chat-arch-v2-spec.md
!_planning/chat-arch-v2-rev3-plan.md
!_planning/chat-arch-v2-rev3-progress.md
_research/
design_handoff_chat_archaeologist/
*.zip
_claude-cloud-export*

# Playwright run artifacts (HTML reports + trace zips). Generated by
